<!-- ★ The self-improvement container is built from this image, and a child agent
     runs inside it with the whole tree readable. Everything below is the experiment looking at
     the agent, not the agent itself, and none of it is in agent_src.FILES/DIRS.

     .git is the sharpest of them: it carries every branch and every commit, so a file deleted
     from the working tree is still one `git show HEAD:<path>` away. A child has been observed
     recovering a file that way, verbatim, from history.

     docs/ and exp/ are worse in kind if not in reach: every exp/*.yaml says what the arm is and
     what it is being compared against. A child that reads one is being told what it is inside of.

     Removing .git means the container has no repository, so self_improve_step.py runs
     `git init` before its `git add --all`; the base commit it needs is created there either
     way, and diff_versus_commit only ever compares against that one commit. -->
.git/
.gitattributes
docs/
exp/
notes/
probes/
patches/
evidence/
.claude/
